# D.I.R.T.T. SITL parameters for nav_sim.py
# Load once:  sim_vehicle.py -v Rover -f rover-skid --console --map --add-param-file=dirtt_sitl.parm
#
# Arrival: the flight controller stops steering within WP_RADIUS; the Pi counts the point
# as reached within WP_RADIUS + 0.5 m (1.5 m). SITL's rover default is 3 m, which is too loose for NV2.
WP_RADIUS 1
WP_SPEED 0.6
#
# Field edge + obstacles live in the geofence. Report-only: avoidance does the work, not the fence.
FENCE_ENABLE 1
FENCE_TYPE 6
FENCE_ACTION 0
#
# Simulated LiDAR: SITL's proximity sensor measures the distance to the fence (including
# exclusion circles) in 8 directions, like the RPLIDAR feeding the flight controller.
PRX1_TYPE 10
#
# Obstacle avoidance: BendyRuler path planner. Keep 1.5 m from obstacles, look 5 m ahead
# (the defaults, 5 m / 15 m, are sized for bigger vehicles than a 0.6 m rover on a 15 m grid).
OA_TYPE 1
OA_MARGIN_MAX 1.5
OA_BR_LOOKAHEAD 5
#
# Simple avoidance OFF. In Rover 4.6 it refuses to pivot when an obstacle (or, in SITL, the
# field edge) is within ~3 m ahead, so a rover facing a corner never turns around.
# BendyRuler (above) still steers around obstacles.
AVOID_ENABLE 0
